 project,
 developed in the M12 Intermodular Project module.
 The project analyzes the needs of a carpentry that is completely analog and wants to catch up technologically.
 Two phases are proposed:
 implementation of an IT system and adoption of digital technologies to become a 4.0 carpentry.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

The system is analyzed from the point of view of the main processes that need to be computerized and taking into account the second phase.
 The most relevant use cases have been chosen and those that best complete the needs of the system in terms of hardware,
 networks,
 systems and applications.
 Two solutions are proposed:
 an implementation of a modern IT system and an extension of it with technologies specific to Industry 4.0,
 such as collaborative robotics,
 IoT components,
 blockchain,
 augmented reality and artificial intelligence.
\end_layout

